1. In the text before Eq. (2): "sparsity measure $I_{p,q}(W) = 1 - d^{\frac{1}{p} - \frac{1}{q}} \cdot \frac{\|W\|_p}{\|W\|_q}$"

2. In Eq. (2): $I_{p,q}(W_i) = 1 - d_i^{\frac{1}{q} - \frac{1}{p}} (\|W_i\|_p - \|W_i\|_q)$

These are indeed different: one uses a ratio $\frac{\|W\|_p}{\|W\|_q}$ and the other uses a difference $(\|W\|_p - \|W_i\|_q)$, and also the exponent signs differ. This is a legitimate concern. The standard PQ index from Hurley & Rickard (2009) uses the **ratio** form, and the ratio form is what would satisfy scale invariance etc. 

